Subject: [PATCH 496/496] [DS4.1] B12X remnants: the L2 prefetch packed-weight
 walk; attention's hooks

linear_segments read a linear's b12x_weight and build_l2_prefetch walked a
packed B12X WO through object_segments. B12X's linear methods and WO packing
set those; with them gone nothing does, and the TileLang WO names its bytes
(l2_segments) whenever the plans are built (only once every layer's WO is
set up). object_segments goes with its two callers.

DeepseekV4Attention's docstring names the kernel hooks that only the TileLang
layer defines now that the base class's B12X implementations are gone.
---
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/attention.py    |  6 +++
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/l2_prefetch.py  | 54 +----------------------
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/nvidia/model.py |  7 +--
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 58 deletions(-)

